# [Minimum Number of Changes to Make Binary String Beautiful](https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-number-of-changes-to-make-binary-string-beautiful/)

## Approach: Greedy

- A binary string is beautiful if every pair of adjacent characters at even and odd indices is equal.
- Since the string length is even, divide it into pairs: `(0,1), (2,3), (4,5), ...`.
- For each pair, check whether both characters are equal.
- If the characters are different, we need exactly one change to make them equal.
- Count the number of such pairs and return the count.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int minChanges(string s) {
        int minChange = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < s.length(); i += 2) {
            if(s[i] != s[i + 1]) {
                minChange++;
            }
        }

        return minChange;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** `O(n)` — We traverse the string once, checking every pair.
- **Space Complexity:** `O(1)` — We use only a constant amount of extra space.
